{"call_id": "0305dfba17e34516844c8ad41b9e7acc", "success": true, "result_file": "/data/nly/Agent-Aware-Trajectory-Level-Query/benchmark/fullbench/runs/natural/GITHUB_REPOS/query1/full-01/results/0305dfba17e34516844c8ad41b9e7acc.json", "row_count": null, "preview": "{\"submitted\": true, \"answer\": \"ANSWER: Approximately 13.8% (19 out of 138) of README.md files belonging to repositories that do not use Python include copyright information.\\n\\nMETHOD:\\n1. From the artifacts_database `contents` table, I selected all files whose path is exactly \\\"README.md\\\" (case-insensitive) or ends with \\\"/README.md\\\" — 204 README.md files across 200 repositories.\\n2. I joined these repositories to the metadata_database `languages` table (178 of the 200 repos had language metadata; 22 were unmatched and excluded). A repository was classified as \\\"does not use Python\\\" if its language_description does not mention \\\"Python\\\" (case-insensitive). Repos with \\\"No language information available\\\" were treated as non-Python (Python is not among their declared languages). This yielded 138 README.md files in non-Python repositories (44 README files belonged to Python-using repos).\\n3. A README was deemed to include copyright information if its content contained the word \\\"copyright\\\" (case-insensitive) or the © symbol: 19 of 138 files matched → 19/138 ≈ 13.8%.\\n\\nROBUSTNESS CHECKS:\\n- Requiring the literal word \\\"copyright\\\" only (no © symbol): 17/138 ≈ 12.3%.\\n- Also counting bare \\\"(c)\\\" notices: 21/138 ≈ 15.2%.\\n- Restricting to repos with explicit (non-\\\"No language information\\\") language metadata: 19/130 ≈ 14.6%.\\n- Repo-level (≥1 README with copyright per repo): 19/135 ≈ 14.1%.\\n\\nAll variants cluster around 12–15%; the headline figure is ≈13.8% (about one in seven).\\n\"}", "truncated": false}
